WEBVTT

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:04.430
Today, we are talking about a basic facial.

00:00:04.684 --> 00:00:05.710
It sounds simple:

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:08.430
cleanse, mask, moisturize.

00:00:08.777 --> 00:00:12.590
But every step has a reason, and the order of the steps has a reason too.

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:17.279
Once you understand the reasons, you know when to do a step, when to skip it,

00:00:17.229 --> 00:00:18.430
and how gentle to be.

00:00:19.065 --> 00:00:20.371
The basic order is:

00:00:20.399 --> 00:00:26.904
cleanse, exfoliate, warm the skin with a warm towel or steam, extractions if needed,

00:00:26.854 --> 00:00:28.211
mask and massage,

00:00:28.429 --> 00:00:32.371
then toner, moisturizer, and sunscreen if it is daytime.

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:36.931
You go from clean, to clear, then to nourishing, and protecting.

00:00:37.565 --> 00:00:39.911
Cleansing is the foundation of every step.

00:00:40.304 --> 00:00:42.951
If the client is wearing makeup, cleanse twice.

00:00:43.342 --> 00:00:46.151
The first cleanse removes the makeup and the sunscreen.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:49.214
The skin around the eyes and lips is very thin,

00:00:49.164 --> 00:00:53.351
so place a damp cotton pad on it for a few seconds to soften the mascara,

00:00:53.619 --> 00:00:55.591
then wipe gently, without rubbing.

00:00:55.926 --> 00:00:59.093
The second cleanse uses a cleanser that suits the skin type,

00:00:59.043 --> 00:01:00.391
to clean the skin itself.

00:01:00.542 --> 00:01:04.551
Skip it, and everything you apply afterwards just sits on a layer of residue.

00:01:05.212 --> 00:01:07.874
Exfoliation removes the layer of dead cells,

00:01:07.824 --> 00:01:10.248
so the skin looks brighter and smoother.

00:01:10.633 --> 00:01:12.248
There are three common kinds:

00:01:12.421 --> 00:01:15.768
enzymes, mild acids, and fine grains.

00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:17.288
Choose according to the skin.

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:21.208
Sensitive, thin skin usually suits a gentle enzyme.

00:01:21.478 --> 00:01:24.648
Thicker, oilier skin can tolerate a mild acid.

00:01:25.019 --> 00:01:28.488
Grains must be very fine, and rubbed very gently.

00:01:28.723 --> 00:01:32.568
Leave it on for the time the brand states, and no longer just to be sure.

00:01:33.195 --> 00:01:34.418
Something very common:

00:01:34.598 --> 00:01:39.249
the skin looks rough, so the therapist exfoliates very thoroughly, several times,

00:01:39.199 --> 00:01:42.658
on top of the acid products the client already uses at home.

00:01:43.154 --> 00:01:45.538
The skin looks smooth and glowing that day.

00:01:45.973 --> 00:01:50.834
But a few days later, it is red and sore, it stings when cream goes on,

00:01:50.784 --> 00:01:53.138
and sometimes it peels in patches.

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:57.338
That is the skin barrier being damaged, and the skin needs time,

00:01:57.288 --> 00:01:59.458
sometimes a few weeks, to recover.

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:04.738
So exfoliate just enough, and always ask first what the client is using at home.

00:02:05.353 --> 00:02:09.060
Next, warm the skin with a warm towel, or steam.

00:02:09.567 --> 00:02:14.020
The aim is the client's comfort, softer skin, and easier cleansing.

00:02:14.528 --> 00:02:17.220
A warm towel is just warm, not hot:

00:02:17.568 --> 00:02:19.300
test it on your own wrist first.

00:02:19.778 --> 00:02:24.660
With steam, place the machine far enough from the face, and don't steam for long.

00:02:25.085 --> 00:02:30.316
For very sensitive skin, skin that is red, or with visible small blood vessels,

00:02:30.266 --> 00:02:31.300
skip the steam,

00:02:31.449 --> 00:02:33.780
or use only a cool, damp towel.

00:02:34.444 --> 00:02:38.274
Extractions are the step most likely to cause harm, if done wrong.

00:02:38.863 --> 00:02:42.937
Only do them if you have been trained, and if the rules where you work,

00:02:42.887 --> 00:02:44.354
and your salon, allow it.

00:02:44.987 --> 00:02:46.274
Always wear gloves.

00:02:46.682 --> 00:02:49.159
Wrap soft tissue around your fingertips,

00:02:49.109 --> 00:02:52.434
then press very gently on both sides of the blackhead.

00:02:52.891 --> 00:02:57.394
No nails, no squeezing hard, and no forcing it out at any cost.

00:02:57.803 --> 00:02:59.394
If it doesn't come out, leave it.

00:02:59.742 --> 00:03:02.834
A few small ones, in a short time, is enough.

00:03:03.473 --> 00:03:06.787
Metal extractors, or anything that can break the skin,

00:03:06.737 --> 00:03:09.808
must be cleaned and sterilized after every client,

00:03:10.078 --> 00:03:11.888
then stored in a sealed pouch.

00:03:12.288 --> 00:03:15.488
The City of Helsinki hygiene guidance also states clearly:

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:18.208
blackhead extractors must be sterilized.

00:03:18.493 --> 00:03:22.688
Lancets are single use only, and only where the rules where you work allow them.

00:03:23.136 --> 00:03:27.488
For the sterilizing steps, watch the lesson on tools after every client again.

00:03:28.128 --> 00:03:29.488
Next comes the mask.

00:03:29.593 --> 00:03:31.008
Choose according to the skin:

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:33.568
clay for oily, congested skin;

00:03:33.848 --> 00:03:38.288
cream or gel masks for dry, dehydrated, or sensitive skin.

00:03:38.764 --> 00:03:43.488
Apply with a brush, evenly, avoiding the eyes, the nostrils and the lips.

00:03:43.843 --> 00:03:45.661
Leave it on for the brand's time,

00:03:45.611 --> 00:03:48.768
and don't let clay dry and crack for too long on dry skin.

00:03:49.285 --> 00:03:51.488
Facial massage helps the client relax;

00:03:51.679 --> 00:03:54.528
some salons do it before the mask, some after.

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:57.168
We will have a separate lesson on facial massage.

00:03:57.834 --> 00:04:01.249
Finally, toner, wiped or patted on gently.

00:04:01.755 --> 00:04:04.153
Then a moisturizer that suits the skin type,

00:04:04.103 --> 00:04:06.609
to hold in water and protect the skin barrier.

00:04:07.185 --> 00:04:11.649
If it is morning, or daytime, apply sunscreen as the very last step.

00:04:12.078 --> 00:04:13.009
And tell the client:

00:04:13.294 --> 00:04:16.747
sunscreen every morning is a very important habit at home,

00:04:16.697 --> 00:04:18.449
especially after exfoliation.

00:04:18.997 --> 00:04:23.102
When using a new product on a client, especially one with sensitive skin,

00:04:23.052 --> 00:04:24.546
or a history of allergies,

00:04:24.894 --> 00:04:28.626
test it first on a small area of skin, as the brand instructs.

00:04:29.052 --> 00:04:33.586
A patch test is no absolute guarantee, but it helps avoid many reactions.

00:04:33.698 --> 00:04:37.266
For more detail, watch the lesson on allergies and chemicals.

00:04:37.824 --> 00:04:40.880
Hygiene in skin care is very easy to overlook.

00:04:41.204 --> 00:04:43.360
Wash your hands before every client.

00:04:43.735 --> 00:04:46.320
Take cream out of the jar with a clean spatula;

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:48.398
never put your fingers in the jar,

00:04:48.348 --> 00:04:51.760
because the whole jar will be contaminated for the clients after.

00:04:52.108 --> 00:04:54.801
Brushes, bowls and tools are single use,

00:04:54.751 --> 00:04:57.840
or cleaned and disinfected after every client.

00:04:58.189 --> 00:05:00.560
Towels, headbands and bed linen:

00:05:00.732 --> 00:05:02.080
fresh for every client.

00:05:02.642 --> 00:05:07.674
If the client's skin reacts, with redness, stinging, a lot of itching,

00:05:07.624 --> 00:05:09.596
or a sting that won't stop,

00:05:09.863 --> 00:05:11.516
stop that product right away.

00:05:12.014 --> 00:05:15.756
Rinse gently with cool water, and apply a cool compress.

00:05:16.084 --> 00:05:18.156
Don't put another product on top to fix it.

00:05:18.762 --> 00:05:22.156
Write down the product name, the batch number, and what happened.

00:05:22.744 --> 00:05:26.156
Swelling of the face or lips, or difficulty breathing:

00:05:26.425 --> 00:05:28.396
call emergency services right away.

00:05:28.671 --> 00:05:30.316
Watch the incidents lesson again.

00:05:30.945 --> 00:05:34.560
So you see, a basic facial doesn't need lots of products.

00:05:34.907 --> 00:05:38.560
It needs the right order, the right pressure, and knowing when to stop.

00:05:39.017 --> 00:05:42.640
In the practice lesson, we will do it step by step, together.

00:05:42.901 --> 00:05:45.760
And now, please take the short quiz below the video.

00:05:46.015 --> 00:05:46.720
See you next time.
